import{_ as t,c as n,o as r,ag as a}from"./chunks/framework.Vyheyqg9.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"n8n errors, tests and deployment ownership","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"applied-ai/n8n/operations.md","filePath":"applied-ai/n8n/operations.md"}'),o={name:"applied-ai/n8n/operations.md"};function i(s,e,d,l,c,p){return r(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="n8n-errors-tests-and-deployment-ownership" tabindex="-1">n8n errors, tests and deployment ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#n8n-errors-tests-and-deployment-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to “n8n errors, tests and deployment ownership”">​</a></h1><p>An execution record shows what n8n observed, not necessarily what a remote service committed. Test the boundary that failed and retain the original event identity before choosing retry or replay.</p><h2 id="errors-and-retries" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">1 </span>Errors and retries <a class="header-anchor" href="#errors-and-retries" aria-label="Permalink to “1 Errors and retries”">​</a></h2><p>An error workflow starts from Error Trigger and is selected in workflow settings. Stop And Error can deliberately fail a run on a policy condition. Manual test executions and automatic/production error workflows have different behavior; do not assume a manual failure proves the production error handler ran. Trigger failures can also provide a different error-data shape. Keep missing execution/reference fields optional in diagnostic projection. <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/flow-logic/error-handling/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official error handling</a>.</p><p>Node Retry On Fail is a bounded attempt mechanism, not business idempotency. Configure attempts and delay deliberately, and account for service/client retries below it. A 401/403, malformed input or conflict is not repaired by repeating it. A 429/503 may permit backoff/defer under the service&#39;s retry hint and total deadline. An ambiguous write timeout needs status reconciliation. “Continue on error” changes the workflow outcome; route its error result explicitly rather than treating it as a normal receipt. Inspect the installed node&#39;s available error/retry settings. <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/workflows/components/nodes/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Node settings</a>, <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.httprequest/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">HTTP node</a>.</p><p>For the reference integration, leave automatic write retries off initially. Test same-key replay at the service boundary first, then allow a small declared retry policy. Rate/admission, per-request timeout, workflow timeout and total elapsed/retry budget are different limits. A timeout cannot forcibly undo an already completed external action.</p><h2 id="testing-and-execution-history" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">2 </span>Testing and execution history <a class="header-anchor" href="#testing-and-execution-history" aria-label="Permalink to “2 Testing and execution history”">​</a></h2><p>Use a synthetic manual input first. Pin/mock safe data for repeatable transformations; production executions do not use development pinning. Inspect zero/one/multiple items and every branch, then use a test webhook with separate test credentials. Pinned success data can conceal a failing downstream service, so unpin it for the actual integration test. <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/data/data-pinning/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pinning/mocking</a>.</p><p>Execution history helps locate the first failed node and compare projected inputs/outputs. Saved payloads may include private excerpts, headers or tokens: minimize fields, restrict readers and define saving/pruning/deletion/backup policy. Re-running old execution data can repeat effects; reauthorize the event and use its original business operation ID. Debug/copy-to-editor features depend on edition/registration; use sanitized fixtures if unavailable. <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/workflows/executions/debug/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Execution debugging</a>.</p><p>Test the custom service independently of n8n, then the installed nodes and credentials, then the complete test-only workflow. A plain JavaScript transform check does not validate n8n expression evaluation, item linking, node versions, webhook registration or credential delivery. Those remain separate learner observations in N8N-P01.</p><h2 id="deployment-basics-without-a-hosted-side-effect" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">3 </span>Deployment basics without a hosted side effect <a class="header-anchor" href="#deployment-basics-without-a-hosted-side-effect" aria-label="Permalink to “3 Deployment basics without a hosted side effect”">​</a></h2><p>For an owned deployment, pin an exact supported image/release and record its digest/platform/configuration. Separate development/test from production credentials and data. Protect the editor, use appropriate TLS/proxy/webhook URL configuration, a least-privilege service identity and restricted outbound destinations. Do not expose a local editor through a tunnel just to make a synthetic test convenient.</p><p>Persist the n8n database/configuration and retain the credential encryption key securely alongside the recovery plan. Losing the key can make restored credentials unusable; in queue mode workers require consistent key configuration. Test a restore into an isolated environment before reconnecting triggers or destinations. A backup file or a workflow JSON export alone is not a tested recovery. <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/hosting/configuration/configuration-examples/encryption-key/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Encryption-key ownership</a>.</p><p>The current official Compose documentation also describes optional Assistant/sandbox services. They are not prerequisites for this small automation; do not enable AI-generated code execution, cloud assistants or additional paid features by copying an unrelated full stack. Review the <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/deploy/host-n8n/install-options/install-using-docker-compose.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current installation guidance</a> against the exact selected version, resources and permitted features. This course supplies a deployment decision contract, not an executed hosting recipe.</p><p>Queue mode, distributed workers, external secrets, SSO, enterprise governance and AI agent/vector nodes are optional later extensions. Evaluate their edition/version requirements separately. The material completion gate is a bounded useful explanation and ready practice; no n8n production activation, paid service or external notification was performed here.</p>',15)])])}const f=t(o,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,f as default};
